{"id": "section-013-example-1", "source_section": "section-013", "context_markdown": "### A. Select two pillows and move those objects

NL: “Move two pillows from the sofa onto the armchair.” No implied heating, cleaning, or extra resources.

", "braincode": "MODE REQUEST
ENTRYPOINT ObjectLabelPillow
TASK ObjectLabelPillow {
  ACTION pick_up(target=object_label::pillow, quantity=2, source=object_label::sofa) -> object_label_pillow_refs : LIST[REF[STRING]]
  FOR EACH item IN object_label_pillow_refs {
    ACTION place(target=item, destination=object_label::armchair, relation=on)
  }
}
", "status": "migrated to value groups (lexical-groups release); source qualifications apply"}
{"id": "section-014-example-1", "source_section": "section-014", "context_markdown": "### B. Preserve the class and amount of an itinerary constraint

NL: “Make a three-day Kyoto itinerary, including at least one temple each day, with at most twenty minutes of walking between stops.”

", "braincode": "MODE REQUEST
ENTRYPOINT Itinerary
TASK Itinerary : STRING {
  TERM content_kyoto_itinerary() -> content_kyoto_itinerary_2 : TERM
  TERM duration(amount=3, unit=unit_day) -> duration_2 : TERM
  TERM minimum_per_period(class=class_temple, count=1, period=unit_day) -> minimum_per_period_2 : TERM
  TERM maximum_between_stops(activity="walk", amount=20, unit=unit_minute) -> maximum_between_stops_2 : TERM
  GENERATE(target=art_itinerary, constraints=[duration_2, minimum_per_period_2, maximum_between_stops_2], topic=content_kyoto_itinerary_2) -> itinerary : STRING
  RETURN itinerary
}
", "status": "copied verbatim; source qualifications apply"}
{"id": "section-015-example-1", "source_section": "section-015", "context_markdown": "### C. Existing constraint symbol becomes a typed construction

NL: “Suggest realistic pickup lines.” This example treats the message as a conversational request for suggestions.

", "braincode": "MODE REQUEST
ENTRYPOINT Conversation
CONVO Conversation {
  TURN t1 SPEAKER=USER {
    TERM constraint_realistic() -> constraint_realistic_2 : TERM
    UTTER ask(constraints=[constraint_realistic_2], topic=topic_pickup_lines)
  }
}
", "status": "copied verbatim; source qualifications apply"}
{"id": "section-016-example-1", "source_section": "section-016", "context_markdown": "### D. Record an actual test outcome without asserting overall correctness

Source manifest: `t1:tests` identifies a supplied agent/tool trace in which the scikit-learn test run exits successfully. The source explicitly reports the selected tests passed; it does not establish that every bug is fixed.

", "braincode": "MODE TRACE
ENTRYPOINT Conversation
CONVO Conversation {
  TURN t1 SPEAKER=AGENT {
    RECORD ACTION run_tests(target=sklearn) STATUS succeeded SOURCE "t1:tests" -> run_tests_event : EVENT
    CLAIM outcome(event=run_tests_event, value=TRUE) BY role_agent STATUS observed SOURCE "t1:tests" -> outcome_2 : CLAIM
  }
}
", "status": "copied verbatim; source qualifications apply"}
{"id": "section-017-example-1", "source_section": "section-017", "context_markdown": "### E. Preserve exact wording through generation and sending

NL: “Write a polite email asking my manager for an update on Project Atlas, and send it.”

", "braincode": "MODE REQUEST
ENTRYPOINT ShortText
TASK ShortText {
  TERM content_status_update(subject="Project Atlas") -> content_status_update_2 : TERM
  GENERATE(target=art_short_text, format=format_email, tone=tone_polite, topic=content_status_update_2) -> short_text : STRING
  ACTION send_email(content=short_text, recipient=role_manager, tone=tone_polite)
}
", "status": "copied verbatim; source qualifications apply"}

{"id": "v19/rule/reading-guide", "version": 2, "symbol": "rule_reading_guide", "kind": "rule", "status": "Retained", "definition": "The spec governs syntax/types; this glossary defines vocabulary. Signature notation: ? optional, A / B explicit alternatives, void no result. Omitted optional arguments are unspecified. Value entries are category-refined STRING primitives; complex meanings require composition. Aliases are contextual hints, not unconditional equivalences. Report ambiguity. IDs use v19/<category>/<symbol>, v19/support/<symbol> or v19/composite/<symbol>. Statuses apply to this candidate: Retained preserves meaning; Adapted uses the stated contract; Composite requires TERM (bare STRING deprecated); Structural is syntax/argument vocabulary; Needs clarification is unusable until resolved; Deprecated is historical; Accepted is usable within this candidate.", "mentions": ["v19/structural-word/STRING"], "core": true}
{"id": "v19/rule/structural-constructs", "version": 2, "symbol": "rule_structural_constructs", "kind": "rule", "status": "Retained", "definition": "Apply spec Sections 2–14 for modes, binding, control, calls, claims, records and canonical form. No extra syntax is introduced by documentation aliases types-lexicon/action/bind. Epistemic and recording statuses are reserved in their grammar positions. SOURCE and lower-case source are distinct; names are case-sensitive. Residual descriptive values cannot hide propositions.", "core": true}
{"id": "v19/rule/operations-general", "version": 2, "symbol": "rule_operations_general", "kind": "rule", "status": "Retained", "definition": "Operations are callable vocabulary, not arbitrary values. Signatures and categories constrain each parameter; extra attributes need a reviewed profile. Bind REQUEST results. Failure creates no successful result; TRACE records failures without fabricated runtime values. Runtime failure handling is outside this profile. No automatic custom_general_<predicate> operation exists."}
{"id": "v19/rule/search-web-attributes", "version": 3, "symbol": "rule_search_web_attributes", "kind": "rule", "status": "Retained", "definition": "Optional filters: availability, category, color, cuisine, currency, gender, genre, location, platform, ram_unit, reservation_availability, shape, size (category-refined STRING); max_price, min_ram, min_rating (NUMBER); trending (BOOL). Explicit signature alternatives additionally admit atoms. Price requires currency; RAM requires a capacity unit; no default scale/source. rank is invalid: use sort, whose rank_field accepts rank_* and rank_direction accepts dir_*. Category/genre/availability accept only their own subfamilies.", "mentions": ["v19/operation-vocabulary/search_web", "v19/attribute-name/cuisine", "v19/attribute-name/ram_unit", "v19/attribute-name/reservation_availability", "v19/attribute-name/min_ram", "v19/attribute-name/rank_field", "v19/attribute-name/rank_direction"]}
{"id": "v19/rule/speech-acts-general", "version": 2, "symbol": "rule_speech_acts_general", "kind": "rule", "status": "Retained", "definition": "UTTER-only, void, with the spec's speech attributes and LIST[TERM] constraints. No result binding. Literal content cannot replace required semantic arguments for structured coverage.", "core": true}
{"id": "v19/rule/recording-signatures", "version": 2, "symbol": "rule_recording_signatures", "kind": "rule", "status": "Retained", "definition": "RECORD ACTION uses the operation signature with REF[STRING] → TERM and LIST[REF[STRING]] → LIST[TERM]; other types/categories stay unchanged. Return EVENT, never the runtime result. Record actual outputs as attributed CLAIMs. Do not infer missing resources.", "mentions": ["v19/operation-vocabulary/run_tests"], "core": true}
{"id": "v19/rule/support-primitives-general", "version": 2, "symbol": "rule_support_primitives_general", "kind": "rule", "status": "Retained", "definition": "Pure TERM constructors assert nothing. Expansion literals are exact identifiers/atomic values, never hidden sentences. Omit unsupported optional arguments. Counts/indices are nonnegative integers; preserve.index ≥ 1; amounts are nonnegative. minimum_per_period.class uses semantic-category-value; period and temporal duration use the temporal duration-unit-value subset. activity verbs have the role-specific meanings defined in their composites; ambiguous new verbs need review and do not create executable operations.", "mentions": ["v19/support/minimum_per_period", "v19/support/activity"]}
{"id": "v19/rule/trace-relations-general", "version": 2, "symbol": "rule_trace_relations_general", "kind": "rule", "status": "Retained", "definition": "Relations cover their published signatures only; recording a success differs from assuming it. No unlisted reasoning relation is implied.", "core": true}
{"id": "v19/rule/composites-general", "version": 2, "symbol": "rule_composites_general", "kind": "rule", "status": "Retained", "definition": "Composites are acyclic TERM expansion templates. $name substitutes the typed argument; fixed strings are semantic atoms. No silent defaults. Emit nested applications as separate TERM bindings; zero-argument calls are allowed only with a published decomposition. Bare legacy STRING use is deprecated. Jazz/classical piano topic labels do not express a separate genre/instrument relationship; decompose when needed. Named works/products are exact referents. Greatest-cricketer topic specifies neither a winner nor a greatness metric. Budget-limited supplies no monetary ceiling. constraint_17_plus retains its reviewed definition; use a numeric age requirement only when the source specifies age, not for an unspecified mature rating. event_* returns narrative TERM, not EVENT; char_* describes a character, not an asserted real person; chg_* describes intent; assert_* describes a test expectation, not success.", "mentions": ["v19/topic-value/topic_jazz_piano", "v19/topic-value/topic_classical_piano", "v19/composite/topic_greatest_cricketer_of_all_time", "v19/composite/constraint_budget_limited", "v19/constraint-value/constraint_17_plus"]}
{"id": "v19/rule/attributes-and-generate", "version": 2, "symbol": "rule_attributes_and_generate", "kind": "rule", "status": "Retained", "definition": "Attribute entries name arguments; legality/types come from each operation, not global membership. GENERATE uses the spec's core fields; retained artifact profiles return STRING. Numeric/list results need explicit profiles. Legacy itinerary fields expand to TERM constraints: duration/duration_unit → duration(amount,unit); stop_min_per_day/stop_requirement → minimum_per_period(class,count,period=unit_day), never an inferred temple class; max_walk_duration/unit → maximum_between_stops(activity=\"walk\",amount,unit). No legacy shorthand is enabled. Old events/character_properties/transformations become explicitly scoped TERM constraints. Message purpose is TERM, not send_email.content: GENERATE exact STRING content, then send. Report opaque fallback separately.", "mentions": ["v19/attribute-name/target", "v19/attribute-name/cuisine", "v19/attribute-name/min_ram", "v19/attribute-name/ram_unit", "v19/attribute-name/reservation_availability", "v19/attribute-name/rank_field", "v19/attribute-name/rank_direction", "v19/attribute-name/quantity", "v19/support/minimum_per_period", "v19/duration-unit-value/unit_day", "v19/support/maximum_between_stops", "v19/operation-vocabulary/send_email"]}
{"id": "v19/rule/supplemental-general", "version": 2, "symbol": "rule_supplemental_general", "kind": "rule", "status": "Retained", "definition": "Supplementary entries obey the same static and RECORD rules. Aliases are empty unless explicitly stated; no undeclared domain vocabulary is implied."}

{"id": "v19/rule/category/entity-name", "version": 1, "symbol": "rule_category_entity_name", "kind": "category_rule", "status": "Retained", "category": "entity-name", "definition": "STRING descriptors select kinds/resources. `mug` is a descriptor, not REF. Resource symbols may be used only when the source explicitly requests such a resource; missing equipment is not automatically inserted.", "mentions": ["v19/entity-name/mug"]}
{"id": "v19/rule/category/search-value", "version": 2, "symbol": "rule_category_search_value", "kind": "category_rule", "status": "Retained", "category": "search-value", "definition": "STRING refinements rank_ / dir_ / cat_ / avail_ / genre_ are separate. rank_rating may fill rank_field; genre_label::comedy may not. “Cheapest” usually requires both rank_price and dir_asc, not rank_price alone.", "mentions": ["v19/search-value/rank_rating", "v19/attribute-name/rank_field", "v19/lexical-group/genre_label", "v19/search-value/rank_price", "v19/search-value/dir_asc"]}
{"id": "v19/rule/category/spatial-relation", "version": 1, "symbol": "rule_category_spatial_relation", "kind": "category_rule", "status": "Retained", "category": "spatial-relation", "definition": "STRING relation used by place. `in` and `on` have different spatial meaning and are not aliases. Orientation requires context when left/right/front are ambiguous.", "mentions": ["v19/spatial-relation/in", "v19/spatial-relation/on"]}
{"id": "v19/rule/category/location-name", "version": 1, "symbol": "rule_category_location_name", "kind": "category_rule", "status": "Retained", "category": "location-name", "definition": "STRING location descriptor. A `table` surface is not the generated artifact category art_table.", "mentions": ["v19/location-name/table"]}
{"id": "v19/rule/category/descriptive-value", "version": 1, "symbol": "rule_category_descriptive_value", "kind": "category_rule", "status": "Retained", "category": "descriptive-value", "definition": "STRING modifier/domain label; never a free-form proposition. dom_sgi needs its intended referent established before semantically dependent use.", "mentions": ["v19/descriptive-value/dom_sgi"]}
{"id": "v19/rule/category/format-value", "version": 1, "symbol": "rule_category_format_value", "kind": "category_rule", "status": "Retained", "category": "format-value", "definition": "STRING format. format_email is layout, not the action send_email.", "mentions": ["v19/format-value/format_email", "v19/operation-vocabulary/send_email"]}

{"id": "v19/rule/lexical-groups", "version": 1, "symbol": "rule_lexical_groups", "kind": "rule", "status": "Accepted", "definition": "Section 3.1 defines value groups: `group::key` values of type ATOM[group]. Open groups admit any key of their form (examples are not whitelists); standard groups admit the codes of their bundled standard (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 for country, ISO 4217 for currency). Leaf values are never glossary entries. Consumer signatures alone decide where a group may appear. Retired bare symbols are invalid.", "core": true}
{"id": "v19/support/lexical_label", "version": 1, "symbol": "lexical_label", "kind": "constructor", "status": "Accepted", "signature": "TERM lexical_label(value: ATOM[object_label] / ATOM[genre_label] / ATOM[food_label] / ATOM[animal_label] / ATOM[color_label]) -> TERM", "definition": "Describe a domain-qualified leaf label using the atom group contract. Adds no inferred properties, relation, assertion or English-sense resolution. A downstream TERM consumer must permit this description role; TERM typing alone never turns a label into a condition or proposition.", "not": "Inferring that cork is waterproof, or using a label as a complete claim.", "dependencies": ["v19/lexical-group/object_label", "v19/lexical-group/genre_label", "v19/lexical-group/food_label", "v19/lexical-group/animal_label", "v19/lexical-group/color_label"], "shared_rules": ["v19/rule/lexical-groups"]}
{"id": "v19/lexical-group/object_label", "version": 1, "symbol": "object_label", "kind": "lexical_group", "status": "Accepted", "definition": "An explicitly supplied label of an object kind; no inferred physical properties or English sense.", "group": {"examples": ["object_label::thimble", "object_label::pillow"]}}
{"id": "v19/lexical-group/genre_label", "version": 1, "symbol": "genre_label", "kind": "lexical_group", "status": "Accepted", "definition": "An explicitly supplied genre label, without inferred genre taxonomy.", "group": {"examples": ["genre_label::comedy", "genre_label::shoegaze"]}}
{"id": "v19/lexical-group/currency", "version": 2, "symbol": "currency", "kind": "lexical_group", "status": "Accepted", "definition": "A currency identified by its ISO 4217 code (currency::ZAR is the South African rand); no exchange rate or implicit conversion.", "not": "A country (use country::<ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code>) or an amount (use measure with a currency unit).", "group": {"admission": "standard", "standard": "iso4217", "key_form": "upper_code", "examples": ["currency::USD", "currency::EUR"]}}
{"id": "v19/lexical-group/country", "version": 2, "symbol": "country", "kind": "lexical_group", "status": "Accepted", "definition": "A country identified by its ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 code (country::JP is Japan). The code names the country only; no language, currency or region membership is implied.", "not": "A language (use a locale value) or a currency (use currency::<ISO 4217 code>).", "group": {"admission": "standard", "standard": "iso3166-1-alpha2", "key_form": "upper_code", "examples": ["country::JP", "country::DE"]}}
